From 362bde6379dbd006e4d7845fc54ffab4ec334d01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tualua <dsp@mvdnet.org>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 13:45:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Wait for the VPP output syncpoint before encoding to avoid
 corrupted frames under concurrent sessions

When several QSVEncC sessions share one GPU, a single frame can be encoded
from a stale input surface: the last mini-GOP anchor before a forced IDR,
silently, with no error or warning. Observed with AV1 10-bit, --avhw with
VA video memory, a P010 VPP stage and B-pyramid, with 2 or more concurrent
sessions on an Arc A380 (Linux). See rigaya/QSVEnc#308.

Wait for the syncpoint attached to the incoming frame in
PipelineTaskMFXEncode::sendFrame() before calling EncodeFrameAsync(). This
serializes the VPP -> encoder hand-off the same way the ffmpeg QSV path
does; the flush call passes no frame and is unaffected.

With this change the corrupted frame appeared in 0 of 60 test iterations
(on 8.31), versus 13 of 40 hot-scene encodes (about a third) without it. The root ordering problem probably lies
below the API (driver/runtime); this is a workaround at the application
level, not a proven fix of the underlying cause.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 QSVPipeline/qsv_pipeline_ctrl.h | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/QSVPipeline/qsv_pipeline_ctrl.h b/QSVPipeline/qsv_pipeline_ctrl.h
index 8911f98a..39e61e37 100644
--- a/QSVPipeline/qsv_pipeline_ctrl.h
+++ b/QSVPipeline/qsv_pipeline_ctrl.h
@@ -2863,6 +2863,11 @@ public:
             PrintMes(RGY_LOG_ERROR, _T("Invalid frame type.\n"));
             return RGY_ERR_UNSUPPORTED;
         }
+        // wait for the VPP output syncpoint before handing the surface to the encoder.
+        // without this, when several sessions share one GPU, the encoder could encode a stale input surface (see issue #308)
+        if (frame) { // frame is nullptr on the flush call
+            frame->waitsync();
+        }
 
         auto bsOut = m_bitStreamOut.get([enc = m_encode, log = m_log](RGYBitstream *bs) {
             mfxVideoParam par = { 0 };
